$\blueD{\text{Line }a}$ has points at $(-5,9)$ and $(-1,-5)$.

>$\begin{align} 
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\\\\\
&= \dfrac{-5-9}{-1-(-5)} \\\\\\
&={\dfrac{-14}{4}}\\\\\\
&=\blueD{-\dfrac{7}{2}}
\end{align}$

$\greenD{\text{Line }b}$ has points at $(2,6)$ and $(4,-1)$.

>$\begin{align} 
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\\\\\
&= \dfrac{-1-6}{4-2} \\\\\\
&=\greenD{\dfrac{-7}{2}}
\end{align}$
